Errors:
  'x > 1MeV': Incompatible units in comparison: length and energy in expression "x > 1MeV"
  'mod(pdgcode,3) == 1': mod(a,b) can not be used with negative values in expression "mod(pdgcode,3) == 1"
  'pdgcode * 1000000000 > 0': Multiplication of integers gives values outside the range of the result (32-bit integers) in expression "pdgcode * 1000000000 > 0"
  'x < 1e400cm': A constant has NaN or infinite values in expression "x < 1e400cm"
  'x > 1e308km': A constant has NaN or infinite values in expression "x > 1e308km"
  'wavelength > 1Aa': The wavelength is only defined for neutrons and gammas, so keep only those before using it, e.g. "pdgcode == neutron; wavelength > 1.8Aa" (in expression "wavelength > 1Aa")
  'pdgcode in (neutron) and ekin/(ekin-ekin) > 0': Division gives NaN or infinite values in expression "pdgcode in (neutron) and ekin/(ekin-ekin) > 0"
  'x': Expression "x" has units (length), so divide it by a unit, e.g. x/cm
  'pdgcode = 2.5': Non-integer values assigned to pdgcode in expression "pdgcode = 2.5"
  'x = 1MeV': Can not assign value with energy to x, which is a length, in expression "x = 1MeV"
  'ekin < 5000 eV + x': Incompatible units in arithmetic: energy and length in expression "ekin < 5000 eV + x"
  'neutron': neutron is a PDG code (2112), not a condition (e.g. pdgcode == neutron), in expression "neutron"
  'pdgcode in (1cm)': Syntax error in expression "pdgcode in (1cm)", after "pdgcode in (1": the values after "in" must be integers or names of particles, as in pdgcode in (neutron,gamma) or userflags in (1,2)
